## BGP ROUTING MODEL

Each fabric is an Autonomous System advertising knowledge prefixes.
The gateway maintains the F-RIB and performs unicast path selection.

  BGP Concept                    | Fabric-SDK Equivalent
  -------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------
  Autonomous System (AS)         | Individual fabric
  Route advertisement            | Fabric's knowledge domain registration
  Local preference               | Confidence score (100 = local fabric, 1 = Claude)
  MED (Multi-Exit Discriminator) | AIANA embedding freshness breaks ties
  Route withdrawal               | Fabric health check failure
  iBGP                           | Fabric-to-fabric (within Tailscale mesh, trusted)
  eBGP                           | Claude (external, different trust, firewall-filtered)
  Default route (0.0.0.0/0)      | Claude — lowest local preference, route of last resort
  Route reflector                | Gateway / fabric-ctrl
  Route aggregation              | Multiple fabric context combined before dispatch

Path selection algorithm:
  1. Check F-RIB for most-specific prefix match to incoming query
  2. If exact match → unicast to owning fabric (local pref = 100)
  3. If two fabrics advertise same prefix → MED: fresher AIANA embeddings wins
  4. If no match → aggregate partial matches + inject context → Claude (0.0.0.0/0)
  5. Claude receives full aggregated context from all contributing fabrics (never cold)
  6. Outcome routed back down → worker executes
  7. AIANA indexes outcome → F-RIB updated if new pattern learned

