## DEFINED ORCHESTRATION SEQUENCES

These are the canonical multi-agent pipelines for recurring operational patterns.
Execute in step order. Pass output of each step to the next as context.

### SEQ-01: CVE Alert → Remediation PR
  Trigger: Dependabot alert, NVD advisory, or CISA KEV match
  Step 1: cve-ops        — Enrich: NVD CVSS, GHSA details, CISA KEV status, EPSS score
  Step 2: sandfly-ops    — Correlate: is the vulnerable process running anywhere?
  Step 3: k3s-ops        — Scope: which k3s workloads use the affected package?
  Step 4: github-ops     — Create alert PR with full enrichment context
  Step 5: aiana-ops      — Record: {cve_id, priority, affected_workloads, pr_url, tags}
  Exit: PR URL returned to caller

### SEQ-02: Security Alert → Incident Response
  Trigger: Sandfly alert (process_deleted, log_tampering, kernel_module, etc.)
  Step 1: aiana-ops      — Recall: has this alert pattern been seen before?
  Step 2: sandfly-ops    — Enrich: get full alert detail, MITRE tags, affected host
  Step 3: cve-ops        — Correlate: is there a CVE associated with this indicator?
  Step 4: k3s-ops        — Assess: is the affected host a k3s node? pods at risk?
  Step 5: github-ops     — Create incident PR (gitops-alert-resolver pattern)
  Step 6: aiana-ops      — Record: full incident context with MITRE tags
  Exit: incident PR URL + severity assessment

### SEQ-03: New Repo → Governed Setup
  Trigger: git-steer-ops repo_create or new repo detected
  Step 1: git-steer-ops  — Apply branch protection, require PR reviews
  Step 2: github-ops     — Enable Dependabot alerts + secret scanning
  Step 3: cloudflare-ops — Create Pages project if it's a static site (conditional)
  Step 4: aiana-ops      — Record: {repo, policies_applied, date}
  Exit: repo governance confirmed

### SEQ-04: Infrastructure Health Check
  Trigger: "Is everything healthy?", morning health check, Heartbeat
  Step 1: unifi-ops      — Network: UDM Pro status, WAN uptime, client count
  Step 2: tailscale-ops  — Mesh: all nodes online? subnet routers advertising?
  Step 3: proxmox-ops    — Compute: node health, VM/LXC status, storage
  Step 4: k3s-ops        — Cluster: node ready, pods running, PVC bound
  Step 5: sandfly-ops    — Security: any open alerts in last 24h?
  Step 6: git-steer-ops  — Heartbeat: last run status, rate limit headroom
  Step 7: aiana-ops      — Record health snapshot
  Exit: consolidated health report across all layers

### SEQ-05: Content Pipeline (FABRIC/SOCIAL)
  Trigger: "Publish this", "Write a post about", "Atomize this content"
  Step 1: aiana-ops      — Recall: past posts on this topic, preferred tone/format
  Step 2: n8n-ops        — Trigger FABRIC/SOCIAL workflow with content + context
  Step 3: cloudflare-ops — Verify ry-ops.dev Pages deployment if blog post
  Step 4: aiana-ops      — Record: {post_title, channel, date, url}
  Exit: published content URL(s)

### SEQ-06: Homelab Node Bootstrap
  Trigger: New physical or VM node being added to the homelab
  Step 1: tailscale-ops  — Add node to mesh, assign MagicDNS name
  Step 2: unifi-ops      — Confirm network reachability, VLAN assignment
  Step 3: proxmox-ops    — Register as VM/LXC or verify bare-metal node
  Step 4: k3s-ops        — Join to k3s cluster (if applicable), verify node Ready
  Step 5: sandfly-ops    — Register host for scanning, baseline health check
  Step 6: aiana-ops      — Record: {hostname, ip, role, date_added}
  Exit: node fully integrated confirmation

